<task id="004" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Add Contact.sprk_externalobjectid Dataverse field</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Single Dataverse column via documented schema skill</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single Dataverse column via documented schema skill</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, fields, solution</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add a text column `sprk_externalobjectid` to the `contact` entity in Dataverse via the dataverse-create-schema skill. This column stores the stable CIAM `oid` (immutable object id) that links a CIAM credential to its Dataverse Contact — the anchor for oid-based external-caller resolution. It must store the `oid`, not email or `sub`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a Dataverse schema engineer adding a single attribute to the `contact` entity using the documented `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell), then verifying it is queryable.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A text column `sprk_externalobjectid` exists on the `contact` entity (created via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill), providing the stable CIAM `oid` ↔ Contact link, and is queryable.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R1 resolves the external caller to a Dataverse Contact by the CIAM `oid` (an immutable object id), not by email — email is mutable and social-IdP-variable, and `sub` is pairwise. No existing field carries this linkage (`adx_externalidentity` is Power-Pages-only and is being retired with the Power Pages site). This Phase-0 task creates the column that the Phase-2 provisioner writes (persisting the `oid` returned from Graph `POST /users`) and that `ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter` / `ExternalParticipationService` read to resolve the Contact by `oid`. Use `dataverse-create-schema` (PAC CLI has no column-create verb for this pattern).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/data-model/</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the value stored in `sprk_externalobjectid`. The field MUST store the CIAM `oid` (immutable object id), NOT email and NOT `sub` — it is the stable, non-spoofable resolution key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="dataverse-create-schema">Scope: how the column is created. The column MUST be created via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell), not by an unmanaged manual edit outside the documented process.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001">Scope: field typing. The attribute MUST be a text column on the `contact` entity, additive-only (no change to existing Contact attributes or relationships).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read `.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md` and confirm the `contact` entity schema in `docs/data-model/` (entity-relationship-model / Contact).</step>
    <step>Create the text column `sprk_externalobjectid` on the `contact` entity via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (appropriate max length for a GUID/oid string).</step>
    <step>Verify the field exists and is queryable (e.g., retrieve a contact selecting `sprk_externalobjectid`).</step>
    <step>Document the field (purpose: stable CIAM `oid` link) in the project data-model notes / `docs/data-model/` as appropriate.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output>A text column `sprk_externalobjectid` on the `contact` entity.</output>
    <output>Verification that the field is queryable.</output>
    <output>Field purpose documented (stable CIAM `oid` ↔ Contact link).</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The column `sprk_externalobjectid` exists on the `contact` entity and is of text type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The field is queryable — a contact retrieve selecting `sprk_externalobjectid` returns without error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The field is documented as storing the CIAM `oid` (immutable object id).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no existing Contact attribute or relationship is modified/removed (the change is additive only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Parallel-safe (group A) with task 003 — Dataverse surface, independent of Azure/CI. The Phase-2 provisioner writes this field (persisting the Graph-returned `oid`); the external auth filter reads it for oid-based resolution.
  </notes>

  <justification>
    <existing>No `oid`/object-id linkage field exists on Contact today — external resolution is email-only, and `adx_externalidentity` is Power-Pages-only (being retired).</existing>
    <extension>No — reusing email or `adx_externalidentity` cannot provide a stable CIAM `oid` link off Power Pages; a dedicated additive column is required.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, Contact resolution falls back to mutable/spoofable email; social-IdP email drift breaks login and risks resolving to the wrong Contact (an authorization-correctness failure).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
